{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And we will not drink water of the well.</b> He stated it for an inclusive ruling, for well-water — it is obvious that we would not drink it, since there is trouble involved in going back and filling up. But even water of a flowing spring (בְּאֵר) where the source overflows of itself and this one benefits and that one loses nothing — even so, we will not drink of yours. And afterward they added and said, ״וְנָתַתִּי מִכְרָם״ — to provide him remuneration. And likewise at the outset they said, ״דֶּרֶךְ הַמֶּלֶךְ נֵלֵךְ״ — the king's road, which the king's way is to travel upon. And he answered, ״פֶּן בַּחֶרֶב אֵצֵא לִקְרָאתֶךָ״, since the road is conquered for the king — for if Esau meets you, who yields before whom? And he answered, ״בַּמְּסִלָּה נַעֲלֶה״."], :book :numbers, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:42:13.913532044Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}